41. Query 41: Is the shortfall in achievement of PSL targets for the year calculated based on the PSL loans outstanding as on March 31st of 
the financial year? 
Clarification: The shortfall/excess in achievement is calculated for each quarter of the financial year. The shortfall/ excess for the year 
is arrived at by taking a simple average of the shortfall/excess for all the four quarters.  
In case of shortfall in achievement of overall PSL target or any of the prescribed sub-targets, the bank will be required to contribute to 
specified funds maintained with NABARD/SIDBI/MUDRA/NHB. 
